\fIqetuto\fR sets up and maintains the GnuPG keyring used to verify
signatures on binary packages, under \fI${ROOT}/etc/portage/gnupg\fR.
It is a C reimplementation of \fBapp\-portage/getuto\fR and drives
\fBgpg\fR(1) and \fBgpgconf\fR(1) directly, so it needs no installed
\fBgetuto\fR.
.P
On each run it imports the Gentoo release keys, refreshes them from the
Gentoo keyserver and Web Key Directory, and sets the appropriate owner
trust, so that \fBqmerge\fR(1) (and Portage) can verify GLEP\ 78 signed
\fBgpkg\fR packages. The operation is idempotent: an already\-current
keyring is left untouched, and the keyring is rebuilt through a staging
directory so an interrupted run cannot leave it half\-written.